From 3197cd239bfd1e1da70b65cfca34b8d1d2678af6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JPyke3 <github@pyk.ee>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:27:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] DRM: run a compositor from the leased output
 (--drm-lease-client)

gamescope --backend drm --drm-lease-client <socket> takes the lease fd a
--lease-connector gamescope hands out over <socket> and runs on it
instead of opening a session: the leased connector is the only one it
sees. It asks for the --ignore-touch-device touchscreen's input with 'I'
and the lessor forwards that input over the same socket (DrmLeaseEvent:
down/motion/up in the touchscreen's normalised coordinates). One
companion holds the lease at a time; another is told 'B' (busy). The
lessee exits when the lessor goes away.

Ported from Armada's 0013 without the drm-lease-v1 protocol it sits on
(no protocol lease holders to refuse the socket for).

Based-on: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/main/packages/gamescope/patches/0013-feat-drm-run-a-compositor-from-the-leased-output.patch
